(
    title: "Codebreaker",
    description: Some("Mastermind on a keypad: the console — or your opponent — hides a three- or four-digit code and you get twelve guesses (eight with the difficulty switch on A), typed on the Keyboard Controllers, with black and white markers grading each digit as right-in-place or right-but-misplaced. The lowest guess count wins across consecutive rounds, players can author codes for each other, and the cart\'s twenty variations also include the matchstick game Nim."),
